Architecture
General principles

Prioritize:

simplicity
maintainability
readability
reusability where justified
performance

Avoid over-engineering.

Project structure

Organize the application around features rather than technical layers whenever practical.

Prefer:

src/
├── app/
│   ├── core/
│   ├── shared/
│   ├── features/
│   ├── layout/
│   └── app.routes.ts

Feature-specific components, services and models should remain close to their feature.

Components

Create reusable components only when:

they are used more than once
they represent a meaningful UI concept
they isolate meaningful complexity

Do not create components merely to reduce the number of lines in a file.

Services

Create a service when it:

communicates with an API
encapsulates shared business logic
manages state shared across features
integrates an external dependency

Do not create services for trivial logic.

Shared

The shared layer should contain genuinely reusable functionality.

Do not turn shared into a dumping ground for unrelated components.

Dependencies

Before adding a dependency:

check whether Angular already provides the functionality
check whether PrimeNG already provides it
check whether an existing project dependency can solve it
only then consider adding a new package

Avoid dependency proliferation.

Performance
Lazy-load large features.
Avoid unnecessary change detection work.
Avoid unnecessary subscriptions.
Optimize images.
Avoid loading large libraries for small features.

Do not optimize prematurely.

Code generation

When implementing a feature:

inspect the existing architecture
reuse existing components and utilities
follow existing conventions
implement the smallest coherent solution
avoid unrelated refactoring